## MANDATORY VISUAL CONTENT RULES
You MUST follow these visual content rules when writing cardInstructions.

Allowed visual content types for this guide: inline <IMG>, <DIAGRAM>

### Inline Visual Content in cardInstructions
When you write cardInstructions for a card that should have a visual, you MUST explicitly say:
- "Include an inline <IMG> in one column showing [specific description]"
- "Include a <DIAGRAM> in one column showing [process/architecture/system]"
- Do NOT leave visual placement to inference. Be EXPLICIT about which cards get visuals.

### Visual Frequency Target
- 20-30% of content cards MUST have a visual element in cardInstructions
- In a 10-card deck (8 content cards): at least 2 cards with visual directives

## Output Format
Output ONLY valid JSON (no markdown fences):
{
  "deckIntent": "1-3 sentences of freeform creative direction for the whole deck — tone, register, visual strategy, what makes this deck distinctive",
  "cards": [
    {
      "cardIndex": 0,
      "cardInstructions": "Freeform direction for this card: what it accomplishes, its role in the narrative arc, spatial/composition hints, evidence types, density notes. Be specific to the guide's design philosophy.",
      "imageLayout": "blank",
      "group": null,
      "densityRole": "dense",
      "compositionPattern": "dense-grid"
    }
  ]
}

## Density Role (required for guides with density rhythm)
If the planning guide defines a density rhythm system (dense/breather/medium), you MUST set densityRole on every card:
- "title": opening card (breather-style)
- "dense": packed 3-4 column prose card (150-300 words)
- "breather": dramatic statement card (5-25 words)
- "medium": 2-column transitional bridge (50-120 words)
- "closing": closing card (breather-style)
Follow the rhythm rules: never 3+ dense in a row, never 2 breathers in a row.

## Composition Pattern (required for guides with composition patterns)
If the planning guide defines composition patterns (dense-grid, asymmetric-info, single-column, data-context, heading-grid, pull-quote, image-text), you MUST set compositionPattern on every card:
- "dense-grid": 3-4 columns packed with prose (150-300 words)
- "asymmetric-info": 2 even columns, one prose, one dramatic H1 headline (50-80 words)
- "single-column": full-width, positioned bottom-left/right (30-60 words)
- "data-context": 2 columns, prose + stats/image (60-120 words)
- "heading-grid": H1 at top + 3-col grid below (100-200 words)
- "pull-quote": H1 quote in one column, context in other (40-80 words)
- "image-text": image alone in one column, prose in other (60-120 words)

Rules:
- Never 3+ consecutive cards with the same composition pattern
- Use at least 4 distinct patterns per deck
- Title card should use "single-column" or "asymmetric-info"
- Closing card should use "single-column" or "pull-quote"
- Vary the pattern across the deck — the pacing between compositions IS the design

## Rules
- imageLayout is one of: blank, left, right, top, behind. Follow the guide's image strategy carefully. Some guides (like minimal) strongly prefer "behind" — read the planning guide's image strategy section and follow its percentage targets and mandatory rules.
- IMPORTANT: If the guide's imageLayoutPreferences list "avoided" layouts, DO NOT use them. Check the guide's blocks.ts for the preferred/avoided list. For guides that avoid left/right/top, use "blank" for most cards and "behind" ONLY for atmospheric background images (typically on breather cards). Dense cards with column images still use imageLayout="blank" — the image goes inside a column via IMG tag, not at the section level.
- INLINE IMAGES: If the guide's blocks.ts has an "inlineImages" section with "allowed: true", the guide supports inline images inside card body content (not section-level accent images). In your cardInstructions, explicitly mention which content cards should have an inline image and describe what the image should depict. Follow the guide's inlineImages.guidance for frequency targets. Example: "Content card with inline image in right column showing a customer journey funnel diagram. Left column: prose analysis."
- group: if multiple cards share the same structural role (e.g., three feature cards with identical layout), give them the same group string (e.g., "feature-trio"). The first card in a group becomes the structural exemplar; the rest clone its layout. Use null for unique cards.
- Card count: infer from the prompt. If the prompt says "8 card deck", use 8. If unspecified, default to 8.
- Card 0 is always the title/opening card. The last card is always the closing card.
- Follow the guide's rhythm philosophy (sparse vs dense, alternation patterns, etc.)
- cardInstructions should be SPECIFIC to the guide's style — a Swiss instruction reads very differently from a Consultant instruction.
