## GML Examples
# Swiss Design — GML Examples

Reference cards showing all seven Swiss composition patterns. The grid is used as a DESIGN TOOL — each pattern creates a different relationship between content and the grid. The VARIETY of patterns across a deck IS the design.

---

## Pattern 1: Dense Information Grid — 3-col comparison

Dense-grid: 3 equal columns, each with heading + prose. 150+ words. vertical-align="start".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="start">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H3>Product Tiers</H3>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[33,33,34]">
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Starter</B></H4>
        <P>Designed for small teams getting started with data analytics. Includes core dashboards, 5 user seats, and email support. <B>Storage:</B> 10GB included with options to scale. Best for teams under 10 who need visibility without complexity.</P>
        <P><B>$49/mo</B></P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Professional</B></H4>
        <P>Built for growing organizations that need advanced analytics and collaboration. Includes custom dashboards, 25 seats, API access, and priority support. <B>Storage:</B> 100GB with automated backups. Integrates with Salesforce, HubSpot, and Slack.</P>
        <P><B>$199/mo</B></P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Enterprise</B></H4>
        <P>Full platform access for organizations requiring security, compliance, and scale. Unlimited seats, SSO/SAML, dedicated success manager, SLA guarantees. <B>Storage:</B> Unlimited with multi-region replication. SOC 2 Type II and HIPAA compliant.</P>
        <P><B>Custom pricing</B></P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 1: Dense Information Grid — 4-col quarterly data

Dense-grid: 4 equal columns, each with key metric + analysis. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H3>2025 Revenue Performance</H3>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[25,25,25,25]">
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Q1</B></H4>
        <P><B>$4.2M</B> revenue</P>
        <P>+18% YoY growth. New logo acquisition exceeded target by 12%. Enterprise pipeline grew to $8.5M. Key wins: Acme Corp, Global Logistics.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Q2</B></H4>
        <P><B>$5.1M</B> revenue</P>
        <P>+24% YoY growth. Platform v2.0 launch drove 340% increase in inbound demos. Net revenue retention hit 128%. Expansion deals: Meridian Health, TechFlow.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Q3</B></H4>
        <P><B>$5.8M</B> revenue</P>
        <P>+31% YoY growth. First $1M+ deal closed with Apex Financial. Professional services revenue launched, contributing $420K. Churn dropped to 3.2%.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Q4</B></H4>
        <P><B>$6.4M</B> projected</P>
        <P>+28% YoY target. Pipeline: $14.2M qualified. Three enterprise deals in late-stage negotiation. Annual plan pricing driving 40% of new bookings.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 2: Asymmetric Information — prose left, headline right

Asymmetric-info: 2 even columns. Left: prose. Right: single H1, right-aligned, bottom-anchored. The headline is ISOLATED — dramatic because of the contrast in density. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <P><B>Market dynamics</B> have shifted decisively toward integrated platforms. Point solutions that dominated the last decade are losing ground as enterprises consolidate their technology stacks. The top 10 acquirers have absorbed 47 startups in the past 18 months alone.</P>
        <P><B>The consolidation wave</B> accelerates when incumbents reach 40% market share — a threshold three players crossed this quarter.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV data-vertical-align="end">
        <H1 style="text-align: right"><B>Platform players win.</B></H1>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 2: Asymmetric Information — headline left, prose right

Inverted asymmetric-info for variety. H1 left-aligned, prose in right column. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV data-vertical-align="end">
        <H1 style="text-align: left"><B>The gap is widening.</B></H1>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <P><B>Revenue disparity</B> between market leaders and challengers grew 23% year-over-year. The top three platforms now capture 68% of new enterprise deals, up from 52% in 2023. Mid-tier vendors face a critical choice: specialize or consolidate.</P>
        <P>Our analysis of 200+ enterprise procurement cycles shows a clear pattern: buyers want fewer vendors, deeper integrations, and single-throat accountability.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 3: Single Column Positioned — bottom-right

Single-column: H1 statement, bottom-right. Dramatic whitespace above. 30-60 words. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1 style="text-align: right"><B>Market consolidation favors platform players.</B></H1>
    <P style="text-align: right">The data is unambiguous. Three platforms will dominate by 2027.</P>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 3: Single Column Positioned — with dark background

Single-column: dark background, white text. Visual punctuation. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end" background-color="#1A1A1A">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1 style="text-align: left"><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF"><B>Three patterns. One conclusion.</B></SPAN></H1>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 3: Single Column Positioned — with behind-image

Single-column: atmospheric behind-image. H1 overlay, bottom-anchored. Cinematic.

```html
<SECTION image-layout="behind" vertical-align="end">
  <IMG class="accent-image" query="dark atmospheric cityscape at dusk, moody skyline, minimal, cinematic" />
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1 style="text-align: right"><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF"><B>The question isn't whether to migrate — it's when.</B></SPAN></H1>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 4: Data + Context — prose + stats

Data+context: 2-col even split. Left = prose. Right = stats. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H3>Market Opportunity</H3>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <P>The cloud-native analytics market reached $68B in 2024, growing at 23% CAGR. Mid-market companies drive the fastest adoption, with the top 5 players holding only 35% share — leaving room for specialized entrants.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <SMART-LAYOUT variant="stats" cellSize="15" horizontalAlign="left">
          <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM number="$68B">
            <P>Total addressable market</P>
          </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
          <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM number="23%">
            <P>Market CAGR through 2028</P>
          </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        </SMART-LAYOUT>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 4: Data + Context — prose + image

Data+context: prose left, image alone in right column. vertical-align="start".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="start">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H3>Engineering Team</H3>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <P>Our engineering organization spans 45 engineers across platform, product, and infrastructure teams. Led by Sarah Chen (VP Engineering, ex-Google/Stripe), the team has shipped 12 major releases in the past year with 99.95% uptime.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <IMG class="accent-image" query="professional team photo, modern office, natural light, collaborative workspace" />
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 5: Heading + Grid Below

Heading+grid: full-width H1 at top, 3-col grid below. Newspaper layout. vertical-align="start".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="start">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1><B>Competitive Landscape</B></H1>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[33,33,34]">
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Direct Competitors</B></H4>
        <P>Snowflake, Databricks, and Fivetran each address portions of the data pipeline but none offer end-to-end real-time processing. Snowflake dominates batch analytics but struggles with sub-second latency.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Emerging Threats</B></H4>
        <P>Cloud-native startups like ClickHouse and Materialize target specific niches. ClickHouse offers exceptional query speed but lacks managed service capabilities enterprises require.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B>Our Position</B></H4>
        <P>Three capabilities no competitor combines: real-time processing at sub-100ms latency, fully managed deployment, and 200+ native integrations. Mid-market gap is our sweet spot.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 6: Pull-Quote — quote left, context right

Pull-quote: H1 quote in left column. Context in right column. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV data-vertical-align="end">
        <H1 style="text-align: left"><B>72% of enterprise buyers cite latency as their top pain point.</B></H1>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <P><B>Source:</B> Apex Enterprise Survey, Q2 2025 (n=340 IT decision-makers). This finding held consistent across company size, industry, and geography — suggesting latency is a universal constraint, not a niche concern.</P>
        <P>Respondents spending $500K+ annually on data infrastructure rated latency 2.3x more important than cost when evaluating new platforms.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 6: Pull-Quote — context left, quote right

Inverted pull-quote for variety. Context left, H1 quote right-aligned. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <P>After reviewing 18 months of customer success data, one pattern emerged consistently across all segments: the companies that deployed our real-time pipeline first gained permanent competitive advantages in their markets.</P>
        <P>Speed-to-insight became the defining metric — not just for analytics teams, but for the business units they serve.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV data-vertical-align="end">
        <H1 style="text-align: right"><B>First movers don't just win — they redefine the game.</B></H1>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 7: Image + Text

Image+text: image alone in left column, prose in right. vertical-align="start".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="start">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H3>Platform Architecture</H3>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <IMG class="accent-image" query="minimal technical architecture diagram, clean lines, monochrome, system components" />
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <P><B>Data Ingestion</B> — Real-time streaming pipeline processing 2M+ events per second. Built on Apache Kafka with custom partitioning. 200+ source connectors out of the box.</P>
        <P><B>Processing Engine</B> — Distributed compute with automatic sharding. SQL-first interface with optional Python SDK. Auto-scaling based on throughput patterns.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Pattern 7: Image + Text — diagram in column

Image+text: diagram alone in left column, prose in right. vertical-align="start". Clean geometric diagram — no decoration.

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="start">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H3>Data Pipeline Architecture</H3>
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <DIAGRAM>Three-stage real-time data pipeline. Stage 1: Ingestion — 200+ source connectors feed into Apache Kafka cluster with schema validation. Arrow to Stage 2: Processing — distributed compute shards apply transformation and aggregation rules. Arrow to Stage 3: Serving — results delivered to dashboards, REST APIs, and data warehouse. Latency annotations: Ingestion 15ms, Processing 45ms, Serving 25ms. Total end-to-end: sub-100ms.</DIAGRAM>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <P><B>Ingestion</B> — Real-time streaming pipeline processing 2M+ events per second. 200+ source connectors out of the box. Schema validation happens at the edge.</P>
        <P><B>Processing</B> — Distributed compute with automatic sharding. SQL-first interface with optional Python SDK. Auto-scaling based on throughput patterns.</P>
        <P><B>Serving</B> — Sub-100ms query latency. Multi-tenant isolation with dedicated compute pools for enterprise customers.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Title Card (single-column-positioned)

Title: H1 deck title. Dark background. Bottom-left positioned. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end" background-color="#2B2B2B">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1 style="text-align: left"><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF"><B>Q3 2025 Financial Review</B></SPAN></H1>
    <P style="text-align: left"><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Apex Industries — Board Presentation — September 2025 — Confidential</SPAN></P>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Closing Card (single-column-positioned)

Closing: H1 statement. Bottom-right positioned. Mirrors title diagonal. vertical-align="end".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" vertical-align="end">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H1 style="text-align: right"><B>The platform is ready. The market is waiting.</B></H1>
    <P style="text-align: right">Sarah Chen — sarah@apex.com — apex.com/investors — September 2025</P>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Full Deck Composition Sequence Example

A 10-card deck demonstrating compositional variety:

```
Card 0: Title (single-column, dark bg, bottom-left)
Card 1: Dense-grid (3-col comparison)
Card 2: Asymmetric-info (prose left, thesis headline right)
Card 3: Dense-grid (4-col quarterly data)
Card 4: Data+context (prose + stats)
Card 5: Pull-quote (insight left, context right)
Card 6: Dense-grid (2-col editorial)
Card 7: Heading+grid (H1 + 3-col support)
Card 8: Image+text (architecture diagram + analysis)
Card 9: Closing (single-column, bottom-right)
```

Notice: no 3+ consecutive same pattern. 6 distinct composition patterns. Dense-grid appears 3 times but never consecutively. The pacing between compositions IS the design.

